# XILINDRO alone in the Corrigida: the controls screen, then a few moves
# with the new keys (`fight_keys_asdf`, `fight_controls_screen`).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame xilindro --headless --ms 18000 --fix all --input tools/play/xilindro-controls.input [--dump DIR]
#
# The screen is up from the start and the round waits: the clock stays at
# 90 and the opponent does not come. Enter takes it down at 1000, PORRADA
# stands for 2 s (`porrada`: nothing moves, the S at 2200 does nothing)
# and the round starts at 3000: the fighter steps in and strikes on
# xilindro-alone-win.input's beats (3000 ms later), with D (high kick),
# A (punch), F (sweep) and S (middle kick) in turn. The punch and the
# middle kick never cost the fighter anything; the high kick and the sweep
# trade with an attacking opponent (docs/xilindro/GAME.md "The fight"), so
# both energy bars get tiles (`kicks`). ↑ (jump) and ↓ (block) follow.
# Closing the window mid-round is a loss (X6).
500 dump controls
1000 key return
2000 dump porrada
2200 key s
3500 dump started
3620 hold right 20
3660 key d
4220 hold left 20
4820 hold right 20
4860 key a
